{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L51-L118","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\nThe substrate parameter $q$ is the variable of the nuclear Skein\npolynomial.  The transfer matrix product computes this polynomial\nin factored form without expansion.\n\n**Proposition.**\n*Let $\\mathcal{N}(Z, N)$ be a nucleus with $A = Z + N$ nucleons.\nThe Markov trace\n([factorization theorem](#thm:markov-trace-factorization))*\n\n$$\n  P_{\\mathcal{N}}(q)\n   := \n  \\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{Markov}}\\!\\bigl(\n    \\mathcal{N}(Z, N)\n  \\bigr)\n  = \n  \\prod_{i=0}^{A-2} \\hat{V}_i(q)\n$$\n\n*is a polynomial in $q^{1/2}$ of degree $\\leq A^2 - 1$.  Each\nfactor*\n\n$$\n  \\hat{V}_i(q) =  z(q) \\cdot a_i(q) + b_i(q)\n$$\n\n*is a rational function in $q^{1/2}$, where $a_i(q), b_i(q) \\in \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$ are the transfer matrix coefficients at\ngenerator $\\sigma_i$ and $z(q) = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})$ is the\nMarkov parameter.  The product $P_{\\mathcal{N}}(q)$ is the\n**Skein polynomial of the nuclear link** in factored form.\nIt is computed by exactly $\\binom{A}{2}$ transfer matrix\nmultiplications — one per nucleon pair.*\n\n*Proof.*\nThe Iwahori--Hecke algebra $H_A(q)$ is defined over the ring\n$\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$.  Each crossing factor\n$C_{ij} = c_j \\sigma_i + d_j$ has coefficients $(c_j, d_j)$\nin $\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$:\n\n| Pair type | $c_j$ | $d_j$ | Hecke element |\n|-----------|-------|-------|---------------|\n| $\\mathfrak{p}$-$\\mathfrak{p}$ | $1$ | $0$ | $\\sigma$ |\n| $\\mathfrak{n}$-$\\mathfrak{n}$ | $1$ | $-(q - q^{-1})$ | $\\sigma^{-1} = \\sigma - (q - q^{-1})$ |\n| mixed | $1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}(q - q^{-1})$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(\\sigma + \\sigma^{-1})$ |\n\nThe $(1, -(q - q^{-1}))$ convention for nn crossings is the unique\nconvention consistent with the Hecke inverse relation\n$\\sigma^{-1} = \\sigma - (q - q^{-1})$.  This is not a normalization\nchoice — any other coefficients break $\\sigma \\cdot \\sigma^{-1} = 1$\nin the standard $(2,1)$ representation.  The unimodularity\n$\\det T = -1$ is a theorem (consequence of the Hecke relation\n$\\sigma^2 = (q - q^{-1})\\sigma + 1$, which forces eigenvalues\n$q, -q^{-1}$ with p\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix","label":"prop:skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_iii_binomial_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_iii_binomial_cost","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (iii): the algorithm performs exactly\n`(A choose 2) = A(A-1)/2` transfer-matrix multiplications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.n_mults","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.n_mults","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Number of transfer-matrix multiplications performed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_ii_degree_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_ii_degree_bound","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii): the degree (in `q^{1/2}`) is bounded:\n`deg(P) ≤ A² − 1` where `A = Z + N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_i_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.claim_i_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i): Markov-trace factorisation\n`P_N(q) = ∏_{i=0}^{A-2} V̂_i(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.degree","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The degree of the Skein polynomial (in `q^{1/2}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.V","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The traced volume `V̂_i(q)` at each generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.P","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The Skein polynomial `P_N(q) ∈ ℝ` evaluated at fixed `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.N","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.Z","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.q","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrixContext","kind":"class","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix.lean#L20-L49","doc":"Abstract context for the `skein_polynomial_transfer_matrix` claim —\nmanuscript-themed typed fields below; sub-claims encode (i) the\ntransfer-matrix factorisation of the Markov-trace Skein polynomial,\n(ii) the polynomial-degree bound, and (iii) the binomial cost\n`(A choose 2)` of the algorithm. ","signatureChunk":0}]}